From 6e3ad5a35b6f55a3451a24f88ed205eb52449897 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fil Dunsky <filipp.dunsky@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 01:53:30 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] net: cortina: integrate reviewed wired IPv4 and IPv6
 flowtable development

Backport the published wired IPv4 RFC and local plain routed IPv6 path.
Preserve bounded RX ownership handling in the preceding basic target.
Retain owner input observations only for a still-active identical original
tuple during refresh, with fresh topology, FDB, neighbour, MTU and format
epoch checks. Reject new unobserved flows or observed ambiguities.
Include reviewed selector-MAC updates, historic bucket refusal ordering,
provider release/teardown, terminal notifier and Kconfig corrections.
Handle stripped QCA4 VLAN metadata and short linear dissection heads;
normalize first-open MTU, avoid redundant CPU replay and propagate QCA
port-status errors without inventing a detach obligation before setup.

Current source passes native ARM vmlinux/modules without the platform or
COMPILE_TEST, exact 6.18 ARM W=1 Werror objects, actual KUnit skb tests
and focused GCC/Clang ASan/UBSan regressions. New corrections have not
been installed on Almond+. Earlier wired IPv4/plain IPv6 hardware
functional evidence does not establish throughput or endurance.

Wi-Fi packet acceleration, general result reclamation and automatic
transient-cut recovery remain incomplete. Active-flow observation expiry
can force a conservative software refresh. Offload mailing rerolls remain
held until basic Ethernet review is completed.

Signed-off-by: Fil Dunsky <filipp.dunsky@gmail.com>
